%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: A Two-Page Document
%%For: pscat
%%Pages: 2
%%EndComments
%% pdf_document.ps — issue #8: a small multi-page "document" (not
%% just a rendered picture) demonstrating `pscat --pdf out.pdf
%% pdf_document.ps`. The %%Title:/%%For: header comments above become
%% the output PDF's /Info metadata (Title/Author), same as gs's own
%% pdfwrite device does with the same two comments — so the resulting
%% file shows a real title in a reader's library (Kindle, Books, any
%% PDF viewer) instead of the bare filename. PDF is already natively
%% accepted by Kindle's Send-to-Kindle (email attachment or USB copy)
%% and virtually every e-reader/PDF viewer, so no separate export
%% format is needed for that half of the issue.

/Helvetica-Bold findfont 28 scalefont setfont
0.15 0.15 0.2 setrgbcolor
90 620 moveto (A Two-Page Document) show

/Helvetica findfont 14 scalefont setfont
0.35 0.35 0.4 setrgbcolor
90 580 moveto (for pscat) show

0.7 0.7 0.75 setrgbcolor
2 setlinewidth
90 550 moveto 522 550 lineto stroke

/Times-Italic findfont 16 scalefont setfont
0.1 0.1 0.1 setrgbcolor
90 480 moveto
(A document, not just a picture: this page and the next are two) show
90 460 moveto
(separate showpage calls, so pscat --pdf emits a real multi-page PDF) show
90 440 moveto
(-- no page outline/bookmarks yet, just real, navigable pages.) show

showpage

/Helvetica-Bold findfont 20 scalefont setfont
0.15 0.15 0.2 setrgbcolor
90 650 moveto (Page Two) show

/Helvetica findfont 13 scalefont setfont
0.3 0.3 0.35 setrgbcolor
90 610 moveto
(This page carries the same document identity \(Title/Author\) as) show
90 592 moveto
(page one -- PDF metadata lives once, at the document level, not) show
90 574 moveto
(per page.) show

0.8 0.3 0.2 setrgbcolor
newpath 300 300 60 0 360 arc fill

showpage
